WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A table seems to move by itself.
Everyone touching it says their hands were still.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In 1853, Michael Faraday asked the question the witnesses couldn't answer:
what moved first?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
His indicator exposed pressure from the hands.
Sincerity and physical causation were separate things.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Modern motion capture finds a related effect with pendulums:
tiny finger motions can become large swings.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
That's an ideomotor phenomenon—
not proof that minds control objects without muscles.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the evidence at Final Vestige.
A vivid experience is the beginning of a question, not its answer.
